LeetCode 151 – Reverse Words in a String

Problem

Reverse the order of the words in a string.

Example:
"the sky is blue" → "blue is sky the"

Approach

Reverse the entire string.

Extract each word.

Reverse that individual word.

Add it to the answer.

Ignore empty words caused by extra spaces.

Example

"the sky is blue"
→ reverse whole string → "eulb si yks eht"
→ reverse each word → "blue is sky the"

Code

class Solution {
public:
    string reverseWords(string s) {
        int n = s.length();
        string ans = "";

        reverse(s.begin(), s.end());

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            string word = "";

            while(i < n && s[i] != ' ') {
                word += s[i];
                i++;
            }

            reverse(word.begin(), word.end());

            if(word.length() > 0)
                ans += ' ' + word;
        }

        return ans.substr(1);
    }
};

Key Concepts

reverse(s.begin(), s.end()) reverses the whole string.

reverse(word.begin(), word.end()) reverses only the current word.

word.length() > 0 skips empty words caused by spaces.

ans.substr(1) removes the extra space at the beginning.

i scans the string and finds words.

Complexity

Time: O(n)

Extra Space: O(n)
